algorithms.pseudocode:
function BerggrenLens(n, d, t):
    if d == 0:
        if Compatible(n, t): return ([], 0)
        else: return (∅, ⊤)
    best_cost ← ⊤; best_path ← ∅
    if Compatible(n, t):
        best_cost ← 0; best_path ← []
    for g in {A, B, C}:
        (path', cost') ← BerggrenLens(n, d-1, g(t))
        total ← w(t, g(t)) + cost'
        if total < best_cost:
            best_cost ← total
            best_path ← [g] ++ path'
    return (best_path, best_cost)

Complexity: O(3^d) time, O(d) space
